WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.7 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Corporate partnerships and sponsorship

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Match each company to the kind of support that fits, and agree the terms.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Be clear: gift, sponsorship, in kind or purchase.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Offer value to them, not only your need.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Check each company against your gift acceptance policy.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Tide Line Youth Collective (Community group · idea stage, Indonesia)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Tide Line: Dive operator A sponsors seedlings and boots for US$2,000, is thanked by name, and has no guests at youth planting days.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write corporate prospects and the support that fits each.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
